    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW21kRXq9R8f9BL3eSYVrQpsh)_\n\nDesign note `docs/architecture/global-keymap-namespaces.org`, modelled on Lambda Emacs' `lem-setup-keybindings.el`. No code or key changes. (Replaces #277, whose branch name had the wrong number.)\n\n- Audit of `sp-keys` and every other binding in `libraries/modules/`: four global collisions (`C-c s l`, `C-c s r`, `C-c m`, `<f6>`), a three-way one on `C-c f`, ten local shadows of global keys (Python and Org mostly), `C-x C-SPC` hiding `pop-global-mark`, and eleven commands in the leader tree with no definition in the repo.\n- Caveats: leader key options, load order and Elpaca timing of `:bind`, terminal and macOS key limits, which-key labels, mode-local overrides, migration shims, and a three-layer test.\n- Design: one `defvar-keymap` per feature module, mounted by `sp-keys` from one registry table; five steps, the first changing no key.\n- README row and CHANGELOG line added.\n\nNot run in Emacs (none in the container). Statements about Emacs defaults are marked \"(memory)\" in the doc and need one check in a real Emacs.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9sdrKxJ3CH27TGGqB)_",
